// 14h FINAL (Mike 10-14: the last table-level videos before the laser goes back up; he's leaning to HOT-BEAM STROBE looks and wants
// stabs + X / Y / Z movement ON THE BEAT). Dark inside the parts = CH1 0 with the look still loaded (as the show does -- the catalog's
// all-zero dark draws the green 3 on every turn-on). PART 1 HOT BEAM / STROBE: 10 PAR + laser pairs (laser latency vs the PARs), flash
// lengths 17-200 ms on dot / line / circles / nodes, strobe 4-20 Hz (45 % on = kitGate), colour + shape swaps (at turn-on, preloaded in
// the dark, while lit), dot size CH5 96-127, CH2 out-of-bounds fragments under spin + shift. PART 2 ON THE BEAT (128 BPM): DMX-stepped
// X (CH7) / Y (CH8) jumps at 1/4 1/8 1/16 lit vs stabbed, corner hops, jump-size ladder (settle time vs distance), rotation snaps (CH6),
// Z = size pops (CH5) + fan snaps (CH10), pattern switches (6 shapes), DMX ramps per 1 beat / 2 beats / 1 bar (beat-locked sweeps instead of the 4 fixed speeds).
// PART 3 SPEEDS: the slow speeds held for whole cycles, swing size, CH5 zoom + CH10 auto speeds. PART 4 WINDOW: a small circle stepped
// through CH7 / CH8 0-124 + an oversized static circle (CH2). PART 5 YOUR LOOKS: every saved scene with laser channels, 6 s each (max
